## Lab-01:

## Title:Hosting a Web Server on the Cloud

## Objectives
1.Access the AWS Console through the sandbox environment
2.Launch an AWS EC2 instance
3.Connect to the EC2 instance and install Nginx
4.Deploy a sample web page
5.Access the hosted web page through a web browser

## Theory/Background
1.Role of Cloud Computing in IoT Systems

Cloud computing provides storage, processing, and management for IoT devices over the internet. IoT devices generate large amounts of data, and the cloud helps store and analyze this data efficiently. It also enables remote monitoring, scalability, security, and real-time access to IoT applications.

Main roles:
-Data storage and processing
-Remote device monitoring
-Scalability for many devices
-Security and backup
-Real-time analytics

2.AWS EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)
AWS EC2 is a cloud service provided by Amazon Web Services that offers virtual servers called instances. Users can run applications, websites, and IoT platforms without buying physical hardware.

Features:
-Virtual servers in the cloud
-Scalable computing resources
-Pay-as-you-go pricing
-Secure and reliable infrastructure
-Supports Linux and Windows systems

Uses:
Website hosting
IoT backend servers
Application deployment

3.Nginx Web Server
Nginx is a high-performance open-source web server used to host websites and manage web traffic. It is fast, lightweight, and supports load balancing and reverse proxy services.

Features:
-High-speed web serving
-Load balancing
-Reverse proxy support
-Low resource usage
-Secure communication with SSL/TLS

Uses:
Hosting websites
Managing API requests
IoT dashboard hosting
Traffic distribution between servers

## Procedure
Step 1: Access AWS Console
Open the AWS Sandbox environment.
Log in to the AWS Management Console.

Step 2: Launch an EC2 Instance
Navigate to EC2 Dashboard.
Click Launch Instance.
Select an Ubuntu Linux AMI.
Choose instance type (e.g., t2.micro).
Create or select a key pair.
Configure security group:
Allow SSH (Port 22)
Allow HTTP (Port 80)
Launch the instance.

Step 3: Connect to EC2 Instance
Use SSH to connect to the instance:
  ssh -i key.pem ubuntu@<public-ip>

Step 4: Install Nginx
-Update packages and install Nginx:
  sudo apt update
  sudo apt install nginx -y

-Start and enable Nginx:
  sudo systemctl start nginx
  sudo systemctl enable nginx

Step 5: Deploy Sample Web Page
-Create a sample HTML page:
  sudo nano /var/www/html/index.html

-Add the following content:
   <html>
   <head>
   <title>My Cloud Web Server</title>
   </head>
   <body>
   -<h1>Welcome to Nginx Web Server on AWS EC2</h1>
   </body>
   </html>

-Save the file.

Step 6: Access the Web Page
Copy the public IP address of the EC2 instance.
Open a web browser.
Enter:
http://<public-ip>
The sample web page should appear successfully.

